From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:21:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] u_threaded_context: reclaim and retry a large buffer upload

tc_buffer_subdata() sends a large, unsynchronized or whole-resource
update through tc_buffer_map() and dropped it when the driver had no
memory for the storage the map needs, without a word: a partial update
of a busy buffer kept the older contents while the memory its own
finished work held was reclaimable. It now gives back what the driver
can, from the thread that owns the context, through u_reclaim, and maps
once more.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c
index ba1764b25b6df0bebfb3caebcfb65ef6115f3f8e..0075a5ef69ca980b9e12e6fe40e7bb688d1ff511 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/util/u_threaded_context.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include "util/u_framebuffer.h"
 #include "util/u_inlines.h"
 #include "util/u_memory.h"
+#include "util/u_reclaim.h"
 #include "util/u_upload_mgr.h"
 #include "driver_trace/tr_context.h"
 #include "util/log.h"
@@ -3218,6 +3219,18 @@ tc_buffer_subdata(struct pipe_context *_pipe,
          usage |= TC_TRANSFER_MAP_UPLOAD_CPU_STORAGE;
 
       map = tc_buffer_map(_pipe, resource, 0, usage, &box, &transfer);
+      if (!map) {
+         /* The driver had no memory for the storage the map needs, and the
+          * upload would be dropped without a word: give back what can be,
+          * from the thread that owns the context, and try once more.
+          */
+         struct u_reclaim reclaim;
+         if (u_reclaim_begin(_pipe, true, &reclaim)) {
+            u_reclaim_settle(&reclaim);
+            map = tc_buffer_map(_pipe, resource, 0, usage, &box, &transfer);
+            u_reclaim_end(&reclaim, map != NULL);
+         }
+      }
       if (map) {
          memcpy(map, data, size);
          tc_buffer_unmap(_pipe, transfer);
